# Overarching App Shell and Navigation

This plan details the implementation of the overarching App Shell, layout restructuring, state management for lessons, and persistent progress tracking.

## User Review Required

Please review the proposed plan to ensure it meets your expectations for the user experience and component structure. 
> [!IMPORTANT]
> The Pyodide WebWorker and `usePyodide.ts` files will remain entirely untouched, as requested.

## Proposed Changes

### Data Setup
#### [NEW] src/data/index.ts
We will create this file to aggregate all the JSON exercises into a single `allExercises` array and export the TypeScript `Exercise` interface.
- Imports `beginner.json`, `intermediate.json`, and `advanced.json`.
- Exports `allExercises` array.

### Progress Tracking
#### [NEW] src/hooks/useProgress.ts
We will create a custom React hook to manage the persistent progress tracking using `localStorage`.
- Initializes `completedExerciseIds` from `localStorage`.
- Exports `markCompleted(id: string)` which updates the local state and syncs to `localStorage`.

### App Shell & Layout
#### [MODIFY] src/app/page.tsx
We will refactor the main page to implement the dark theme split-layout and act as the central state manager.
- Adds state for `activeExerciseId` (defaulting to `allExercises[0]`).
- Integrates `useProgress()`.
- Renders a Left Navigation Sidebar (280px wide) containing a scrollable list of lessons.
- Renders `CheckCircle2` (green checkmark) next to completed lessons in the sidebar.
- Highlights the currently active lesson.
- Renders the `<Workspace />` component in the main content area, passing `activeExercise` and an `onSuccess` callback.

### Workspace Refactor
#### [MODIFY] src/components/Workspace.tsx
We will update the Workspace component to be driven by props instead of the hardcoded `EXERCISE` constant.
- Updates component signature to accept `exercise` and `onSuccess` callback.
- Removes the hardcoded `EXERCISE` object.
- Removes the hardcoded "Dataset Preview" HTML table.
- Adds a `useEffect` that listens for changes to the `exercise` prop. When the user switches exercises, the `useEffect` will:
  - Reset the Monaco Editor's value to the new `exercise.starting_code`.
  - Call `reset()` from `usePyodide` to clear previous output and errors.
  - Reset `activeTab`, `showSuccess`, and `gradingFeedback` states.
- Triggers the `onSuccess` callback when `submitAndGrade` returns a `'passed'` status.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1. Run `npm run dev` and open the app in the browser.
2. Verify the presence of the 280px sidebar populated with all exercises.
3. Click through multiple exercises and confirm that the Markdown instructions and Monaco Editor's starting code update immediately.
4. Verify that running Pyodide code works perfectly for different exercises.
5. Submit a correct solution for an exercise, confirm the success banner appears, and verify the sidebar updates instantly with a green checkmark next to the exercise.
6. Refresh the page and confirm the green checkmark persists (localStorage is working).
